  "authority": "Written only by tools/verification/m01-pacing-golden-amendment.mjs --write (x86); never edited by hand. Derived from git (the replaced golden and the BEFORE simulation are read from beforeCommit) and two runs of each golden route through the same test pilot.",
  "reason": "Owner playtest 2026-10-18, P2: long stretches with nothing to do, a forced real-time wait for 06:00 and unclear objectives (bridge defence; Bąk to the medic). Mission flow changes, in the order a route meets them: (1) objective panel and status text (pacing.interludes, clearer hold_access/hold_corridor texts, pacingStatus); (2) continuity cues only with their objective active and >= 20 real s apart; (3) seg_hold 05:34-05:59 runs at 24x while the player holds the deck after the raid; (4) the west charge waits for Bąk and Dudek to be west of x -90, not at the station, and seg_climax 06:12-06:44 runs at 30x once everyone is west; (5) the roll call finishes a carry still under way (the 07:05 fade). Historical battle-clock times, the 12 objectives, CP-A..D, survivors and 07:05 are the invariants checked per route.",
